    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Modularity functions are then deﬁned for both the positive and negative components as: Q± = ij[Wij± − Pij±]δ(gi,gj). The choice of how to combine the two components to obtain the total modularity is left up to the user, though a number of weighting schemes have been proposed (G´mez et al., 2009; Rubinov and Sporns, 2011). In general, the total modularity is of the form: Q = c+Q+ − c−Q−, where c± are constants. Thus, modularity maximization for signed networks can be viewed as an attempt to maximize the modularity of positive connections while penalizing negative connections when they fall within"
